3.7.4 The Company Interconnection Facilities and the System Upgrades shall be designed, constructed, and installed in accordance with applicable Interconnection Studies and Good Utility Practice, and shall be sufficient, as built and designed, to deliver the full energy Electricity output of the Facility to the Transmission System and to enable the Facility to receive energy and capacity necessary to satisfy its operational requirements.
3.7.5 Generator reserves the right, upon written notice to Company, to suspend at any time all work by Company associated with the construction and installation of the Company Interconnection Facilities, System Upgrades, or both.  In such event, Generator shall be responsible for the costs which Company incurs (i) in accordance with this Agreement prior to the suspension and (ii) in suspending such work, including any costs incurred in order to perform such work as may be necessary to ensure the safety of persons and property and the integrity of the Transmission System and, if applicable, any costs incurred in connection with the cancellation of material and labor contracts which Company cannot reasonably avoid; provided, however, that, prior to canceling any material or labor contract, Company shall obtain Generator’s Generator's written authorization.  Company shall invoice Generator pursuant to Article 5 and agrees to use its best commercially reasonable efforts to minimize its costs.  In the event Generator suspends the performance of work by Company pursuant to this section and has not requested Company to recommence such work required hereunder on or before the three hundred and sixty-fifth (365th) day after such requested suspension first annual anniversary thereof, this Agreement shall be deemed terminated as a result of abandonment by Generator as provided in Section 2.1.2.
3.7.6 Attached as Appendix D is a schedule of milestones for the engineering, procurement and construction of the various facilities of the Parties pursuant to this Agreement, including the projected commercial operation date of the Facility.
3.7.6   Company shall inform Generator on a monthly basis, and at such other times as Generator reasonably requests, of the status of the construction and installation of the Company Interconnection Facilities and System Upgrades, including, but not limited to, the following information, in each case relative to the milestones on Appendix D:  (i) progress to date; (ii) a description of scheduled activities for the next period; (iii) the delivery status of all equipment ordered; (iv) and the identification of any event which Company reasonably expects may delay construction of, or increase the cost of, Company Interconnection Facilities and/or System Upgrades.  In the event that Generator reasonably determines at any time that Company will, for reasons unrelated to any default or delay by Generator, be unable to complete the Company Interconnection Facilities and System Upgrades in a timely fashion so as to allow testing and interconnection of the Facility by the projected commercial operation date (as such may be amended from time to time by mutual agreement of the Parties), the Generator may, upon written notice to Company, pursue any or all of the following remedies: (A) an order requiring specific performance by Company of its obligations under this Agreement from a court of competent jurisdiction; (B) such relief as may be available at FERC; (C) an award from an arbitrator(s) pursuant to the dispute resolution provisions hereof allowing Generator to "step in" and complete the construction of the Company Interconnection Facilities and System Upgrades on Company's behalf, subject to reasonable indemnification of Company as provided herein and (D) such other remedies as may be available at law or in equity, subject to the limitations on remedies and damages otherwise provided for herein.  Company agrees that time is of the essence to Generator in connection with achieving the commercial operation date in a timely fashion in order that Generator may comply with its project agreements and financings for the Facility, and Company hereby waives any objection it may or can have to conducting any proceedings by Generator to obtain any of the foregoing remedies on an expedited basis.
